docs {
  # GET /v1/measuring-points/{id}/readings

  Lower-level drill-down: one MeasuringPoint, segmented by device, with one
  month-end reading per month of the `from`/`to` range and the billable
  `period_consumption` per segment. Nothing finer than monthly.

  Use this when you want finer control than `GET /v1/usage-units/{id}/consumption`
  (which aggregates across all MeasuringPoints of a unit). Output shape is
  the same `measuring_points[0]` node you would get back there, just
  directly addressable.

  ## Default `id`

  `7c8eb987-8018-40e0-8480-ea1527eeee80` = **WE 01 / water_warm** (Musterstraße 2-4) —
  shows the meter-replacement scenario: two device segments in 2025, the
  device was replaced on 2025-06-12.

  ## Query parameters

  - `from` — ISO-8601 date, inclusive; widened to the first day of its month
  - `to`   — ISO-8601 date, inclusive; widened to the last day of its month,
    capped at the last completed month
}
